{title: A New Song}
{subtitle: Psalms 149:1–4}
{key: D}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] | [D] | [D] | [D] |
| [A] | [Bm] [F#m] | [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Praise the LORD with a [A]new song
His [Bm]praise in the assembly of the [G]faithful
Let [D]Israel rejoice in his [A]Maker
Let [Bm]the children [A]of Zion ex[G]ult in their [D]King
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sing to the LORD a new [A]song
[Bm]Praise him with dancing and [G]sound
[D]Tambourine and lyre ring [A]out
For he de[G]lights in his [D]people
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The humble are crowned with sal[A]vation
Let [Bm]the faithful exult in [G]glory
[D]Sing for joy upon your [A]beds
[G]For the [A]LORD has made you [D]new
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bm]Exaltation of [F#m]God in their mouths
[G]A two-edged sword in their [D]hands
[Bm]Vengeance on the [F#m]nations
[G]Punishment on the [A]peoples
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[D]A new song to the [A]LORD
[G]Praise in the assembly
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
